package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"review.diffCoverage reports 0 changed decision lines for this change: the js/bash MC/DC engines do not instrument QML, so the new id-scan loop (Menu.qml:796-803) and the restoreSelection ternary (Menu.qml:791) have no coverage fact either way. This is 'not measured', not 'covered'. The only executing evidence is test code: the upstream vm test in menu-test.sh that runs the extracted setActiveMenu/goBack against a stub model, and the dogfood live compositor witness; their outcomes are not observed in this package (test_outcome_unobserved:SW-REQ-260922-DE93).","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":791},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":796},{"id":"code_mcdc_coverage","kind":"check"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"high","title":"Coverage cannot show the restore branch executing: the changed QML has no instrumented decision lines","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent (effects_unavailable): the call/effect analysis covers C/C++ only, so no new-callee, gained-effect, caller-chain or new-mutable-state facts exist and no uncodified connection could be detected. The effect notes below come from reading the code, not from the engine.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":778}],"severity":"info","title":"Acknowledged: change-effects analysis did not run for this QML change","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"Read in the evaluated tree: the only navStack readers/writers are the push in setActiveMenu (Menu.qml:783), the pop in goBack (Menu.qml:813-815) and the resets in openExistingMenu (Menu.qml:916) and openDmenu (Menu.qml:945), so the new shape does not leak to other code. It did break one pre-existing dogfood witness that asserted `.navStack[0] == \"root\"` (menu-compositor-test.sh:359, updated in this mirror). Anything outside Menu.qml that inspects navStack (debug/state dumps, IPC) would see the new shape. The engine did not analyze new state here (effects unavailable).","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":77},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":783},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":916},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":945},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh","kind":"file","line":359}],"severity":"medium","title":"navStack entries change shape from a menu id string to a {menu, index, itemId} record","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:setActiveMenu","shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:goBack"],"scenario":"type a filter in root, Enter on a drilldown result submenu, then Backspace/Left: which root row holds the cursor?"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"setActiveMenu() is also reached from activateIndex() while a filter is active (Menu.qml:842). The pushed index is then an index into the FILTERED row list, and the itemId may be a deeper drilldown row that is not a direct child of the menu being restored. On Back the filter is cleared, the id scan finds nothing, and the cursor lands on the filtered-list index in the unfiltered list, i.e. an arbitrary row. Needs a test to settle whether that is acceptable or should fall back to the drilled-into menu's own row.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":842},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":791},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: where does the cursor land after Back when the submenu was entered from a filtered search?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Back after drilling in from a filtered search\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:setActiveMenu","SW-REQ-260922-Z48F","SW-REQ-260922-3JG5"],"scenario":"drill from root row N into a submenu, make row N disabled (guard flips) or remove it, then Back: cursor must not rest on a disabled row and must not jump to 0"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"If the remembered row is now disabled, the id scan skips it (rowSelectable guard) and the restored index goes through settleCursor(), which moves forward to the next selectable row; if the id is gone, the saved index is kept (clamped by rebuildDisplay). Neither case is exercised by the PR's tests; Z48F (never rest on a disabled row) and 3JG5 (no cursor when all rows disabled) depend on it.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":797},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":590},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z48F","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3JG5","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: does the restore still honour disabled rows and missing ids?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Back when the remembered row is disabled or removed\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:setActiveMenu","shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:loadProviderForMenu"],"scenario":"Back into a volatile provider-backed menu whose rows are re-enumerated asynchronously and reordered: does the cursor end on the remembered itemId?"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"setActiveMenu() runs the id scan right after rebuildDisplay(), then calls invalidateVolatileProvider()/loadProviderForMenu() (Menu.qml:804-805). For a provider-backed (volatile) parent, rows can arrive later via swapProviderRows -> rebuildDisplay -> settleCursor, which keeps only the index; if the provider reorders or has not loaded yet at restore time, the cursor may not follow the remembered item.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":804},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":410},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-EFNR","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: is the id-follow lost when the parent menu's rows come from a provider that reloads on Back?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Back into a volatile provider-backed menu that reorders\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:goBack"],"scenario":"in a live shell: cursor to a non-first root row, Enter into its submenu, press Left (and separately Backspace): cursor returns to that row"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The PR author states the graphical session was unavailable and Enter->Left / Enter->Backspace was not verified live. The key handler routes both keys to goBack() only when the filter is empty (Menu.qml:1218). The dogfood mirror adds a live compositor assertion for Backspace (menu-compositor-test.sh:365) but no Left-arrow case, and no test outcome is observed in this package.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1218},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh","kind":"file","line":365},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: does Enter then Left/Backspace restore the row in a running Omarchy Shell?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Live Enter->Left and Enter->Backspace in the compositor suite\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"DE93 says Back retraces the menu path; P708 says back navigation retraces the drill path and the cursor never rests on a disabled row. Neither states that Back returns the cursor to the drilled-from row, or that it follows that row by id across reorders. That is the PR's purpose, so the spec is incomplete rather than the code: add a child requirement under P708 (or amend DE93) and trace setActiveMenu/goBack to it.","refs":[{"id":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":778}],"severity":"medium","title":"Cursor restore on Back has no requirement of its own","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708 is in review.changes (code_changed, matchLevel file).","status":"confirmed"}},{"claim":{"params":{"candidate":"unmapped_code|review/pr-13012.diff","path":"review/pr-13012.diff","position":"noise"},"type":"unmapped_code"},"detail":"The file is the dogfood review record of the upstream diff (fetched for the re-audit), added alongside review/pr-13012-reaudit.md; it is not code the product runs and is not part of upstream PR #13012. Position noise: no requirement should trace it; excluding review/ from code scope would stop it being counted.","refs":[{"id":"review/pr-13012.diff","kind":"file","line":1}],"severity":"info