 judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:8c8ef78d02f69fb017980c3a1814fd1ed0415dae9eb1ec04dacee6d494bfc8bc","packageIdentity":"epkg-a908779176b2b4bec75d45616ea112d207622a5571051f68493448070827abba","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"Small, local QML change whose restore logic has no measured coverage and no observed test outcome; edge cases (filtered drill-in, disabled/missing row, async provider rows) are untested, and readiness stays blocked by pre-existing findings."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":5,"rationale":"Settles where the cursor lands when the saved index belongs to the filtered list.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":842}],"title":"Back after drilling in from a filtered search"},{"forClaim":6,"rationale":"Pins Z48F/3JG5 interaction with the restore (next selectable row; saved index, not 0).","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":797}],"title":"Back when the remembered row is disabled or removed"},{"forClaim":7,"rationale":"Shows whether id-follow survives asynchronous provider rows.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":804}],"title":"Back into a volatile provider-backed menu that reorders"},{"forClaim":8,"rationale":"Covers the author's unverified manual step; add a Left-arrow variant next to the Backspace witness.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh","kind":"file","line":365}],"title":"Live Enter->Left and Enter->Backspace in the compositor suite"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #13012 makes Back (Left/Backspace) in the menu return the cursor to the row you drilled in from: setActiveMenu() now saves {menu, index, itemId} on navStack and goBack() restores it, following the item by id if parent rows reordered. The mirror also carries dogfood proof work: a stored copy of the upstream diff and a re-audit note under review/, a hardened extraction in menu-test.sh, a navStack-shape fix plus a live restore check in menu-compositor-test.sh, and the node replay mirror.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** Not by coverage: the changed QML has no instrumented decision lines, so the restore branch has no coverage fact. The evidence is test code (the upstream vm test that runs the extracted functions on a stub, and the dogfood live Backspace check), but no test outcome is observed in this package (test_outcome_unobserved). The author did not verify Enter->Left/Backspace live.\n\n**Questions for a human.** Where the cursor lands after Back from a filtered-search drill-in; restore when the remembered row is now disabled or gone; id-follow for provider-backed menus that reload asynchronously; the live Left-arrow path.\n\n**Traceability.** The change is traced function-level to SW-REQ-260922-DE93, but no requirement states the new cursor-restore behaviour: add a child of SYS-REQ-260922-P708 (or amend DE93). review/pr-13012.diff is an unmapped review artifact (argued noise). Effects analysis did not run for QML.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** Readiness is blocked (pre_existing_only): all 28 blocking disclosures (18 failed checks, 10 missing obligations) pre-date the change with baseline delta unchanged; next decision is an investigation by the change_author under the approved policy."}
